    "stdout_tail": "{\"type\":\"result\",\"subtype\":\"success\",\"is_error\":false,\"api_error_status\":null,\"duration_ms\":259439,\"duration_api_ms\":171040,\"ttft_ms\":3487,\"ttft_stream_ms\":2648,\"time_to_request_ms\":85,\"num_turns\":14,\"result\":\"All tests pass.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Summary of what changed:**\\n\\n**File:** `internal/cli/export.go`\\n\\n**Function:** `(d checkpointBranchDestinations) BranchesFor`\\n\\n**Bug:** The function returned the metadata branch (`\\\"feature/something\\\"`) immediately when it was non-empty, skipping the `DefaultCheckpointIDs` reachability check. So checkpoints recorded on a feature branch were still filed under that branch folder even after the branch was merged into the default branch.\\n\\n**Fix:** Moved the `DefaultCheckpointIDs` reachability check to the top of the function, before the metadata-branch fallback. Now, if a checkpoint is reachable from the default branch (meaning it was merged), it is always filed under the default branch folder regardless of what branch the metadata says it was originally recorded on. The original branch is still preserved in `SourceBranch` via `addSelectedSession`.\\n\\n**Validation:** `go test ./internal/cli/ -run \\\"TestExport|TestSnapshot|TestBranchDest|TestBuildBranch|TestBranchesFor|TestListAll|TestDiscover|TestCheckpoint\\\"` \u2014 all 19 targeted tests pass. Full suite: `go test ./internal/cli/ -count=1` \u2014 passes.\",\"stop_reason\":\"end_turn\",\"session_id\":\"c3f5de72-c8a9-4e87-9fc1-80ee0e8130f0\",\"total_cost_usd\":1.0318275000000001,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":13,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":106698,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":784535,\"output_tokens\":10416,\"server_tool_use\":{\"web_search_requests\":0,\"web_fetch_requests\":0},\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":106698,\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0},\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\",\"iterations\":[{\"input_tokens\":1,\"output_tokens\":298,\"cache_read_input_tokens